---
source: apps/oxcruise/tests/cli.rs
expression: table.stdout
---
correctness (default: error)
  circular-dependencies                Reports dependencies that are part of a circular chain of imports.
  cross-package-relative-dependencies  Reports relative imports that reach into another workspace package, for example `../other-package/src/x`.
  dependencies-on-tests                Reports a non-test module that imports a test file or a test directory.
  dev-dependencies-in-production       Reports a production module that imports a package from `devDependencies` only.
  undeclared-packages                  Reports imports of installed npm packages that no `package.json` section declares.
  unresolved-dependencies              Reports an import that oxcruise cannot resolve to a file or a package.

suspicious (default: warn)
  deprecated-dependencies              Reports imports of deprecated Node.js built-in modules and deprecated npm packages.
  duplicate-packages                   Reports a package that more than one `package.json` section declares, for example both `dependencies` and `devDependencies`.
  orphan-modules                       Reports modules that no other module imports and that import no module.

style (default: off)

restriction (default: off)
  layers                               Enforces a layered architecture: a layer can import only the layers that `allow` lists for it.
  optional-dependencies                Reports use of optional dependencies.
  peer-dependencies                    Reports use of peer dependencies.
  visibility                           Restricts access to `internal` directories, as the Go language does.

nursery (default: off)
  unused-exports                       Reports exports that no other module imports.
  unused-modules                       Reports source modules that no path from an entry point reaches.
  unused-packages                      Reports a package that a `package.json` declares and that none of its modules imports.

16 rules
